{"name":"Sky Pilot","hex":"#a2bad4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky pilot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clergyman, especially a military chaplain or padre.","A polemonium, especially Polemonium eximium."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky_pilot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hobo","blocks":[{"text":"A hobo is a migrant worker in the United States. Hobos, tramps, and bums are generally regarded as related, but distinct: a hobo travels and is willing to work; a tramp travels, but avoids work if possible; a bum neither travels nor works."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Hobos2.jpg/330px-Hobos2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hobo"},{"title":"Military chaplain","blocks":[{"text":"A military chaplain ministers to military personnel and, in most cases, their families and civilians working for the military. In some cases, they will also work with local civilians within a military area of operations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Austrian_military_hospital_WWIb.jpg/330px-Austrian_military_hospital_WWIb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_chaplain"},{"title":"Sky Pilot (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sky Pilot\" is a 1968 song by Eric Burdon & the Animals, released on the album The Twain Shall Meet. When released as a single the song was split across both sides, due to its length (7:27). As \"Sky Pilot \" it reached number 14 on the U.S. pop charts, number 15 on the Canadian RPM chart, number 7 on Canada's CHUM Chart and number 40 on the UK singles chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d8/Sky_pilot_-_45rpm_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_Pilot_(song)"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Riding_on_the_rods.jpg/500px-Riding_on_the_rods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Riding_on_the_rods.jpg/500px-Riding_on_the_rods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two men riding underneath a freight train, 1894","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARiding_on_the_rods.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/1909-11-02_Tie_game_A.jpg/500px-1909-11-02_Tie_game_A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/1909-11-02_Tie_game_A.jpg/1280px-1909-11-02_Tie_game_A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/1909-11-02_Tie_game_A.jpg/500px-1909-11-02_Tie_game_A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hobo depicted walking along a railroad on a 1900s card","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1909-11-02_Tie_game_A.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Beggersignsinfrance-sept1921.jpg/500px-Beggersignsinfrance-sept1921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/